Unfortunately,  data‐dependent  problems have been known to sneak
into networks and remain undetected for long periods of time.  In
many cases the particular pattern  that  will  have  problems  is
something  that  doesn’t have sufficient ‘‘transitions’’, such as
all ones or all zeros, or a pattern right at the  edge,  such  as
almost  all zeros.  It isn’t necessarily enough to specify a data
pattern of all zeros (for example) on the  command  line  because
the  pattern  that  is of interest is at the data link level, and
the relationship between what you type and what  the  controllers
transmit can be complicated.  This means that if you have a data‐
